mains wiring. Apart from this, the environment of BACS net-
works is not particularly noisy, especially in of ﬁce buildings.
Reviewing these requirements, peer-to-peer, event-driven
communication schemes appear well suited to BACS.Medium access control using deterministic Carrier Sense,
Multiple Access (CSMA) variants, possibly supporting
frame prioritization, will allow ef ﬁcient use of the “raw”
throughput capacity available as well as ful ﬁll timeliness
requirements for the lower levels.
This is different when compared to industrial automa-
tion, where high-speed control loops favor time-drivenmaster –slave approaches. Also, regarding fault tolerance,
the focus typically is on redundant design (if necessary)
rather than graceful degradation of functionality as systems
need every sensor, actuator or controller to be operational tofulﬁll their purpose.
