Each clusters consists of only the sensors, actuators, and a base
station which are involved in the control loop of an application
for a speciﬁc area. The sensor/actuator nodes communicate
in single-hop1with a base station and retrieve acknowledg-
ment messages per transmission. Based on this architecture,
we assume a star topology in which all the nodes of the
same cluster can communicate with the base station (in which
the controller is running) of the cluster. Contemporary long-
range communication technologies, such as low-power wide-area [42], are representative examples of embodiments this
architecture. Furthermore, the controller, which computes the
control signals, is executed in the base station. In this paper,the terms controller and base station are used interchangeably.
Our communication schemes ar e applied within each cluster
while the information exchange among different clusters is out
of the scope of this paper. Note that, despite the single-hop and
centralized communication, the triggering of state transmissionis distributed for decentralized ETC mechanisms.
A. Simplistic TDMA Protocol
TDMA is a channel access method for shared medium
networks, which allows several users to share the same fre-
quency channel. Speciﬁcally, time is divided into intervals T
i
with length T, so-called superframes. Each interval is split
into smaller time slots Sj, with/summationtextN
j=1Sj≤T,w h e r e Nis
