C. Physical Control System
We consider a LoRa network with nwireless control loops
ℓ1, ℓ2,···, ℓn, where ℓirepresents the feedback control loop
between a sensor node siand actuator aithrough a controller
at the gateway. For a control loop ℓi, the controller computes
control command ui(k)upon receiving state information xi(k)
from sensor si, and then sends it to the actuator ai. The
controller also computes the sampling period for each loop.
We model the physical plant as a linear time-invariant
system (LTI). We use an LTI representation since it models a
wide variety of systems with satisfactory accuracy. A control
loopℓiis represented in the discrete state space as follows.
